1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
On Floriańska Street every bin is emptied
three times a day, full or empty.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,500
Kraków's 9,383 street bins
run on a calendar,

3
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:15,000
not on need.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:19,500
Trash Fairy is a waste collection brain.
A resident scans the QR code on the bin.

5
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:25,000
We accept a report only from that bin's
code and within 150 metres of it.

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Three steps, an optional photo. We strip
EXIF, Claude Vision assesses the bin,

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,500
and a rule assigns "AI verified"
or "To be reviewed".

8
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:40,000
AI never rejects a report.

9
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:44,000
The panel on the bin reads from afar:
fill level, next pickup

10
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:48,000
and what goes in.

11
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:53,000
The driver sees bins by priority,
each with a reason: how many reports

12
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:57,500
and how full. The forecast says
when the bin will cross 85%.

13
00:00:57,500 --> 00:01:03,000
"On my way" navigates inside the app,
no switching to maps.

14
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:08,000
"Emptied" closes the report
with one tap.

15
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:14,000
The resident sees a timeline:
received, in progress, done.

16
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:20,000
The city dashboard, on demo data.
Last 30 days: cost PLN 70.4k,

17
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:26,000
minus 2.7%, PLN 4.1k saved
and 668 fewer trips than planned.

18
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Old Town project:
13% fewer pickups,

19
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:36,500
response time from 6.3 to 2.7 hours.

20
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:42,000
In simulation, empty trips
drop from 57 to 27%,

21
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:48,000
shelter overflow
from 338 hours to zero,

22
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:54,000
and across Kraków that's
PLN 1.5 to 2.8 million a year.

23
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:57,000
Kraków doesn't need more bins.

24
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:00,000
It needs a fairy.
